Synfact (https://github.com/GSM1980/synfact-dev), commit 1a6d0c74469db4c30423be29c90e0b07ba7f8003, mods/arp-st.
GPL-2.0-or-later, GSM1980 and contributors, on elekloader by irpina.

Changes for SyntHack on OS 1.42:
- OS 1.41 addresses translated with tools/build/port_source.py 1.42 (85). The ASCII command tags ARP1 and
  CFG1 look like addresses and were put back by hand.
- persist.c is not used: the settings of each audio track are saved with the project (../glue.c, mods/projstore)
  instead of with the Sound; persist.h declares that interface.
- locks.h, view.c: MODE, SPEED, RANGE and LEN lock as one packed native lock on the Sound's spare logical
  index 0x46 (../glue.c) instead of the shared lock service of Synfact's LFO3 (lanes 0x60..0x63). LEN takes
  56 of its 128 values.
- module.c: no SOUND_META (Sound lifecycle) subscription; MAIN blocks counted in arp_frame stand for the host's
  machine telemetry; the view's memory comes from the OS heap. Lines marked "SyntHack:".

